<title>UK: ATHLETICS-BRITISH HURDLER TESTS POSITIVE - NEWSPAPER.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-BRITISH HURDLER TESTS POSITIVE - NEWSPAPER.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Matthew Douglas has tested positive for the banned stimulant ephedrine, a British newspaper reported.</p>
<p>Sunday's Observer said 20-year-old Douglas, 1995 European junior 400 metres hurdles bronze medallist, was tested at an indoor meeting in January and faced a ban of three months.</p>
